2026-09-08T12:35:00Z ADVANCED - FIRST ROADMAP-TIER UNIT. Tiers 1-2 empty (0 open critical/high) so D-014 priority finally reached tier 3, the plan. Built + dispatched embed-provider-seam (U1.1, plan section 10 Phase 1), the head of the vector layer - U1.2-U1.5 all block on it and packages/index/src/vector does not exist. Committed 3bacdaa. DESIGN CALLS: embed() is OPTIONAL on Provider because claude-code runs a CLI and Anthropic ships no embedding API - requiring it would force four adapters to implement a method that throws, a worse lie than not implementing it; the router SKIPS incapable members rather than failing the chain on its first one, and records the skip as an attempt but NOT as a failed job. Gemini uses batchEmbedContents and Ollama /api/embed, both over the EXISTING Transport so this is one more HTTP shape not a second SDK and the existing fake covers it. Ollama matters beyond fallback: it is what keeps goal.md "never leak the corpus into a public model" reachable, since chunking every transcript is the largest volume of Vidysea text that would ever leave. TWO SILENT-CORRUPTION MODES REFUSED rather than tolerated: a short response (zipping by index attaches one chunk meaning to another chunk id and every later search is subtly wrong with nothing to show) and a ragged one (differing lengths cannot be compared by cosine so dims would be fiction). At the router, no capable provider is an ERROR not an empty result - an index build that SUCCEEDS while producing nothing is the hardest failure to notice. LIVE: 2 vectors, 3072 dims, gemini-embedding-001, 0.8s, cosine 0.8178 between distinct sentences. 11 new tests; pnpm -r test 380 passing / 0 failing across 8 packages; typecheck 0; depcruise 0 violations / 269 modules. DISCLOSED not implied: no vectors stored (chunks still has embeddingRef, a string pointer, not a vector field - that is U1.2), nothing calls embed() in production (U1.3), and Ollama live path untested since nomic-embed-text may not be pulled - naming the untested path is the previous unit lesson applied.
